No user-facing change: more error contracts are declared as rejection
manifests rather than written as unit tests, so each is expanded across
the languages its gates admit and its message is kept in a golden file.
Several of those expansions found languages the hand-written lists had
missed. A manifest can now pass ``None`` for an option whose default is
a member, declare ``variable_form = "both"``, and take the case's value
as an option member's name.
